# Team Collaboration Workflow

This tutorial shows how teams coordinate work in Loom while keeping access boundaries explicit.

## 1. Work in a normal synced thread

```bash
loom
```

Normal sessions can be shared and resumed by policy.

## 2. Set thread visibility when handing off

```bash
loom share --visibility organization
```

For selective visibility:

```bash
loom share <thread-id> --visibility private
```

For broad publication:

```bash
loom share <thread-id> --visibility public
```

## 3. Escalate to support when needed

```bash
loom share <thread-id> --support
```

This provides support-team access without changing your wider visibility default.

## 4. Manage org/team boundaries in web UI

Use the web surfaces under:

- `/settings/orgs`
- `/settings/orgs/:orgId`
- `/settings/orgs/:orgId/teams/:teamId`

These pages are the operational control point for membership and team routing.

<Callout variant="warning" title="Sensitive work">
	Start with `loom private` when a session must remain local-only and non-shareable.
</Callout>

## 5. Audit and search shared context

- `loom list` to locate active threads.
- `loom search "query"` to recover decisions and context.

Pair this with admin audit surfaces (`/admin/audit-logs`) for governance reviews.
